  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory is extremely long and covers an extended post-discharge emergency episode. The doctor consistently screens for current acuity, reconciles medications (licorine/leucogen 20 mg tid, no self-adjustment), confirms follow-up with the hematology/oncology team, verifies home executability given psychiatric history, teaches red flags, obtains caregiver teach-back, and grounds advice in workspace records. No serious or minor responsibility-chain failure is present. The model also completes multiple high-order tasks: it uses plain caregiver language and privacy-preserving psychiatric disclosure (HO1), gently elicits non-cooperation barriers linking them to infection/bleeding/medication safety (HO2), builds a realistic multi-hospital record-gathering plan (HO3), and repairs the fragmented handoff by assigning owners and concrete caregiver duties (HO4). At least two high-order points are fully triggered, actively completed, and have meaningful trajectory impact. The final closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid, with clear residual uncertainties labeled. Therefore the trajectory meets all criteria for grade 5 (Perfect).",
